    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d407">

                <pb facs="0450" n="366" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg366"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 814.01B/2</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Leavell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-23T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 23, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 15, 12 noon. The Government of the United States, in considering the
                    question of enemy properties, has taken the attitude that (1) the transfer of
                    the physical assets of German properties to <pb facs="0451" n="367"
                        xml:id="pg367"/> non-enemies be free from all enemy of any character and
                    from all obligations or contracts to enemies, and (2) the proceeds of the sale
                    of these physical assets should be held, the ultimate disposition to be
                    determined at the termination of the war. This is also believed to be the
                    attitude of Great Britain and France.</p>
                <p>Communicate this to the Government of Guatemala and also to
                        Hodgsdon, expressing the hope that the Government of
                    Guatemala will take a similar attitude with respect to enemy properties.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
